doc:admin_approve_award_2012_05_03 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund approval of award to company A. (3 May 2012)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2012-05-03"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_sdif_approve_award_2012_05_03 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Following the notification of the outcome of the tendering process to the Radio and Television Supreme Council and the Competition Authority, on 3 May 2012, the Fund approved the award of Viva TV-Radio Viva to company A. for the price of USD 5,000,000."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_auction_2011_02_08 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Auction for Viva TV-Radio Viva (8 February 2011)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2011-02-08"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_a_auction_2011_02_08,
        doc:participation_sdif_auction_2011_02_08 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "However, only company A. participated in the auction held on 8 February 2011. Company A. initially submitted a bid of USD 3,750,000, after which the tendering process proceeded to the next stage of open bidding. Company A. then increased its offer to USD 4,150,000."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_award_2011_02_11 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund award of Viva TV-Radio Viva to company A. (11 February 2011)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2011-02-11"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_a_award_2011_02_11,
        doc:participation_sdif_award_2011_02_11 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 11 February 2011, during the negotiation phase, company A. raised its bid to USD 5,000,000. As a result, Viva TV-Radio Viva was awarded to company A."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_consolidate_radio_viva_2007 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Consolidation of Radio Viva assets into single economic unit"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:admin_establish_units_2007_07_19 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_sdif_consolidate_radio_viva_2007 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "A similar resolution was adopted regarding Radio Viva. The Fund decided that the seized assets, rights, properties and associated components utilised by Radio Viva, including contracts and the rights arising therefrom, would also be consolidated into a single economic and commercial unit."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_consolidate_viva_tv_2007 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Consolidation of Viva TV assets into single economic unit"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:admin_establish_units_2007_07_19 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_cine_dijital_consolidation_2007,
        doc:participation_company_cinebes_consolidation_2007,
        doc:participation_company_erdem_consolidation_2007,
        doc:participation_company_kutyay_consolidation_2007,
        doc:participation_company_multikanal_consolidation_2007,
        doc:participation_company_spor_cocuk_consolidation_2007,
        doc:participation_sdif_consolidate_viva_tv_2007 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "With respect to Viva TV, the Fund resolved to consolidate all seized assets, rights, properties and associated components, such as contracts and the rights arising therefrom, belonging to debtor companies within the Erol Aksoy Group and effectively used by Viva TV into a single economic and commercial unit. This consolidation encompassed the following companies: Cinebeş Filmcilik ve Yapımcılık A.Ş., Cine Dijital İletişim Hizmetleri Ticaret A.Ş., Kutyay Özel Radyo Televizyon Yayıncılık A.Ş., Spor ve Çocuk Televizyon Reklamcılık ve Yapımcılık A.Ş., Erdem Radyo Televizyon Yayıncılığı ve Reklamcılık A.Ş., and Multikanal Dağıtım ve Ticaret A.Ş."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_merge_2009_07_09 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision to merge Viva TV and Radio Viva (9 July 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2009-07-09"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_sdif_merge_2009_07_09 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 9 July 2009, the Fund decided to merge the two economic and commercial units, thereby creating the Viva TV-Radio Viva Economic and Commercial Unit (hereinafter referred to as “Viva TV-Radio Viva”)."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_negotiation_2011_02_10 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision to continue tendering by negotiation (10 February 2011)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2011-02-10"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_a_negotiation_2011_02_10,
        doc:participation_sdif_negotiation_2011_02_10 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "As this bid was below the estimated value, 10 February 2011 the Fund decided to continue the tendering process through negotiation."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_non_enforcement_decision_2015_10_27 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision that annulment could not be enforced (27 October 2015)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_general_assembly_2015_07_07 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2015-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_erol_non_enforcement_notification_2016_04_18,
        doc:participation_sdif_non_enforcement_2015_10_27 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 18 April 2016, the Fund notified the applicant of a decision taken on 27 October 2015 regarding the impossibility of enforcing the judgment. The Fund clarified that, at the time of the invitation to tender and subsequent process, there had been no injunction, stay of execution or any other court order preventing the process. The tendering process had proceeded with the necessary approvals from the relevant authorities. The Fund further explained that the tender amount had been collected and Viva TV-Radio Viva had been transferred to the bona fide successful bidder. The funds obtained had been used to settle outstanding debts with certain creditors, and, since then, the Fund no longer exercised control over the asset in question. In the light of these circumstances, the Fund concluded that the enforcement of the annulment decision was not practicable, as rescinding the tendering would not restore the prior legal and factual status and would infringe the acquired rights of the successful bidder. Therefore, the Fund determined that the annulment decision could not be enforced, in terms of both legality and practicality."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_offer_sale_2007_08_29 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision to offer Viva TV and Radio Viva for sale (29 August 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2007-08-29"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_sdif_offer_sale_2007_08_29 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 29 August 2007, the Fund resolved to offer both Viva TV and Radio Viva for sale together in a single tendering process, setting a reserve price of USD 8,000,000. However, as no bids were received, the tendering process could not proceed."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_offer_sale_2009_11_05 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision to offer Viva TV-Radio Viva for sale (5 November 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2009-11-05"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_p_2009_11_05,
        doc:participation_sdif_offer_sale_2009_11_05 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 5 November 2009, the Fund resolved to offer Viva TV-Radio Viva for sale, establishing a reserve price of USD 6,000,000. Although a company, P. A.Ş., obtained the tender documents with the intention of submitting a bid, the tendering process was subsequently postponed."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_offer_sale_2011_01_13 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision to offer Viva TV-Radio Viva for sale (13 January 2011)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2011-01-13"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_sdif_offer_sale_2011_01_13 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 13 January 2011, the Fund decided to offer Viva TV-Radio Viva for sale again, setting the reserve price at USD 6,000,000. Three companies acquired the tender documents. However, only company A. participated in the auction held on 8 February 2011."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_transfer_management_2008_09_18 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Transfer of management and control of Erol Aksoy Group companies to the Fund (18 September 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:admin_default_determination_2008_04_03 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2008-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_anadolu_transfer_2008_09_18,
        doc:participation_company_erdem_transfer_2008_09_18,
        doc:participation_company_kutyay_transfer_2008_09_18,
        doc:participation_company_medya_transfer_2008_09_18,
        doc:participation_sdif_transfer_2008_09_18 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 18 September 2008, the Fund further resolved to transfer the management and control of all companies within the Erol Aksoy Group to itself, along with the rights of their shareholders, except for the entitlement to dividends."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_transfer_ownership_2012_05_09 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Transfer of ownership of Viva TV-Radio Viva to company A. (9 May 2012)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2012-05-09"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_company_a_transfer_2012_05_09,
        doc:participation_sdif_transfer_2012_05_09 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 9 May 2012, company A. deposited the tender amount into the Fund’s bank account. On the same day, the parties signed the “Agreement on Takeover of Viva TV-Radio Viva” and the Fund transferred the ownership of Viva TV-Radio Viva to company A."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_valuation_2007_08_01 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "TSKB valuation report (1 August 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:tskb ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2007-08-01"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_tskb_valuation_2007_08_01 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 1 August 2007, the Industrial Development Bank of Türkiye ( Türkiye Sınaî Kalkınma Bankası A.Ş ., hereinafter referred to as “TSKB”) issued a report and determined that the value of the Radio Viva Economic and Commercial Unit (hereinafter referred to as “Radio Viva”) was 4,258,000 United States dollars (USD), while the value of the Viva TV Economic and Commercial Unit (hereinafter referred to as “Viva TV”) was USD 373,400."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_valuation_2009_06_30 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "TSKB valuation report (30 June 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:tskb ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2009-06-30"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_tskb_valuation_2009_06_30 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 30 June 2009, a valuation report issued by TSKB determined that the value of Radio Viva was USD 5,782,000 and the value of Viva TV was USD 132,000."^^xsd:string .

doc:case_58919_18 a echr:CaseDocument ;
    rdfs:label "CASE OF EROL AKSOY v. TÜRKİYE (Application no. 58919/18)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasApplicant doc:partyErolAksoy ;
    echr:hasApplicationNumber "58919/18"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasDomesticProceeding doc:enforcement_non_enforcement_by_sdif_1,
        doc:proceeding_annulment_valuation_tender_sale_1 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the application (no. 58919/18) against the Republic of Türkiye lodged with the Court under Article 34 of the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms (\"the Convention\") by a Turkish national, Mr Erol Aksoy (\"the applicant\"), on 5 December 2018;"^^xsd:string .

doc:liquidation_protocol_1 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Liquidation Protocol (terms)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Section 9 of the Liquidation Protocol set out the conditions for default, specifying that in the event of a default by any of the joint debtors, all other debtors would be deemed to have defaulted as well."^^xsd:string,
        "Under the terms of the Liquidation Protocol, the debtors undertook joint and several liability for all present and future debts and their ancillary obligations."^^xsd:string .

doc:proceeding_admin_first_instance_2011_02_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Proceedings initiated by the applicant before the administrative court (7 February 2011)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:supremeAdministrativeCourt ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_erol_admin_2011_02_07,
        doc:participation_sdif_admin_2011_02_07 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2011-02-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 7 February 2011, the applicant initiated proceedings before the administrative court, contesting the actions of the Fund concerning the tendering of Viva TV-Radio Viva, in which he claimed to hold both direct and indirect shares. He alleged that the Fund had proceeded with the sale without providing him with prior notification and that he had only learned of the sale upon its publication in the Official Gazette. The applicant sought the annulment of all measures related to the sale, including the Fund’s decision of 13 January 2011, which approved the invitation to tender and the terms of sale and set the estimated value of Viva TV-Radio Viva at USD 6,000,000."^^xsd:string,
        "The applicant attached those documents, emphasising that the buyer had been made aware of the possibility of a lawsuit to annul the sale prior to participating in the auction and negotiations."^^xsd:string,
        "The applicant contended that, in line with well-established case-law, as affirmed by the Court of Cassation, the buyer and its representatives could not be considered bona fide third parties."^^xsd:string,
        "he had sent identical notifications to both the buyer company, company A., and its owners on 7 and 9 February 2011, respectively."^^xsd:string .

doc:proceeding_constitutional_enforcement_1 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Proceeding before the Constitutional Court concerning enforcement and failure to enforce annulment judgments"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:enforcement_non_enforcement_by_sdif_cine5_1 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:constitutionalCourt ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeClaimGranted ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionFavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_erol_constitutional_enforcement_1,
        doc:participation_sdif_constitutional_enforcement_1 ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeConstitutional ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Accordingly, the Constitutional Court concluded that the applicant had exhausted all available remedies."^^xsd:string,
        "As to the admissibility of the individual application, the Constitutional Court observed that the annulled administrative decisions had rendered the sale of the economic and commercial unit retroactively invalid and emphasised that legal or practical difficulties could not exempt the administration of its duty to enforce court judgments."^^xsd:string,
        "The Constitutional Court concluded that the administration’s failure to enforce the annulment decisions amounted to a violation of the applicant’s property rights under Article 35 of the Constitution."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:isFinalDomesticDecision true .

doc:proceeding_rectification_rejection_2016_01_25 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Proceeding: Supreme Administrative Court rejection of Fund's request for rectification (25 January 2016)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_general_assembly_2015_07_07 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:supremeAdministrativeCourt ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-01-25"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeClaimDismissed ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_erol_rectification_2016_01_25,
        doc:participation_sdif_rectification_2016_01_25 ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 25 January 2016, the Supreme Administrative Court rejected the Fund’s request for rectification, noting that the case had become final following the appeal and was no longer subject to rectification."^^xsd:string .

doc:turkishGovernment echr:hasSupportingQuote "The Government were represented by their Agent at the time, Mr Hacı Ali Açıkgül, former Head of the Department of Human Rights of the Ministry of Justice of the Republic of Türkiye."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:isRepresentedBy doc:repHaciAliAcikgul .

doc:admin_default_determination_2008_04_03 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Fund decision of default and to initiate legal proceedings (3 April 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:savingDepositInsuranceFund ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2008-04-03"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_debtors_default_2008_04_03,
        doc:participation_sdif_default_2008_04_03 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 3 April 2008, the Fund concluded that the Erol Aksoy Group had failed to fulfil several commitments and obligations set out in the Liquidation Protocol, rendering the Protocol no longer effective for the recovery of public receivables. Consequently, the Fund decided to rely on its provisions concerning default. It resolved to initiate legal proceedings against all natural and legal person debtors within the Erol Aksoy Group and to proceed with the sale of assets, including those consolidated as an economic and commercial unit."^^xsd:string .

